  "answer_to_user": "The theme resolves cleanly to a Uranium & Nuclear-Fuel-Cycle megatrend (miners + enrichment/fuel, not just reactor utilities). Across markets the core players: Cameco (CCJ.US, ~$45B) is the anchor, with NexGen Energy (NXE.US, ~$7.3B), Uranium Energy (UEC.US, ~$6.3B), Energy Fuels (UUUU.US, ~$3.7B), Denison Mines (DNN.US, ~$3.2B), Ur-Energy (URG.US), Uranium Royalty (UROY.US) and enCore Energy (EU.US) on the mining side. On the enrichment / fuel-technology side you get Centrus Energy (LEU.US, ~$3.5B), BWX Technologies (BWXT.US, ~$14B) and Lightbridge (LTBR.US). The London listings mirror much of this (Cameco 0R35.LSE, NexGen, Denison, Energy Fuels) with BHP tagged as a secondary uranium exposure. Coverage note: Kazatomprom (the Kazakh state uranium giant) doesn't resolve to a clean listing in the data, though China National Uranium (001280.CS, ~$21B) shows up as a related state name."
